---
description: overpower build methodology — classify the task, then use the right amount of process
alwaysApply: true
---

This project uses **overpower**. Before acting on any build/coding request:

1. Read `skills/using-overpower/SKILL.md` and follow it — it classifies the task
   into a tier (T0 trivial → T3 program) and routes it.
2. Load other skills by opening `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` when named.
3. On a resumed session: read `.overpower/progress.md` then
   `.overpower/findings.md` first.

Cursor specifics (see `SUPPORT.md`):
- **delegate** = a Cursor background agent. Use one per task for parallel groups;
  otherwise implement inline.
- No guard hook — check every edit's path stays inside the worktree yourself;
  `reviewing-changes` is the backstop.

Non-negotiables: classify the tier first; never claim done without verifying;
never act on a delegate result with no concrete run artifact; `progress.md` is
append-only; `findings.md` is never truncated; merge/push/delete/spend need
explicit user approval.
